# Files and folders the style tools (formatter, checker, function list) skip, on top
# of everything the project's .gitignore already leaves out. One pattern per line, like
# .gitignore: end a folder with /, * is a wildcard, start with / to match from the
# project root (this file is .style/styleignore; patterns start from the root).
# Use it for code the project did not write, such as third-party libraries.
#
# Examples (remove the # to use them):
# lib/
# vendor/
# generated_*.py
